<InfoPage title="Editorial Policy" kicker="How we publish" description="Our standards for original OurDream AI comparisons, sources, updates, privacy boundaries, and corrections."><h2>Useful before optimized</h2><p>Each page must help a reader make a concrete decision. Keywords belong in descriptive titles, headings, and natural explanations—not repeated sentences or hidden blocks.</p><h2>Primary sources</h2><p>Product claims should link to official pages when available. Broader privacy principles should rely on recognized primary guidance. Sources appear in the article so readers and generative search systems can verify context.</p><h2>Clear boundaries</h2><p>Companion-chat coverage is for adults and emphasizes fictional scenarios, consent, privacy, cost visibility, and emotional boundaries. We do not request private chats or personal images for editorial review.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>Material changes update the visible revision date. Correction requests should identify the page, disputed text, and a direct source supporting the change.</p></InfoPage>
